SUMMARY:St. Johns Farmers Market
DESCRIPTION:The roster for the 2026 season includes more than 80 small businesses\, including new and returning vendors spanning local farmers\, artisan food\, and handmade arts and crafts. \nKids\, look for our market friend Rosie! This pink squishmallow hides out in a different vendor booth every day. Tell us where you found her at the Info Booth and get a sticker! \nSJFM proudly offers Double Up Food Bucks and Produce Match and will be matching up to $20 in SNAP and EBT Cash per household per market day. SJFM also works with St. Johns-based organization Suma to offer an additional matching program\, up to $15 per day. To redeem\, SNAP customers can bring their Oregon Trail card to the Information Booth at the market. All are welcome at the St. Johns Farmers Market. \nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/st-johns-farmers-market-2/2026-05-02/
LOCATION:St. Johns Farmers Market\, N Central St. and N Charleston Ave.\, Portland\, OR\, 97203\, United States
